From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Frida Hou <Frida-a@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 22:14:45 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] [QW38] gdn recover fold: fold (not drop) pending records of
 non-spec rows, in every cache group

Prefill / non-spec rows read their state with the prefill kernels, not the
fold verify. 0037 dropped any records still pending in their
request-table rows, and only in the first cache group's builder (groups
built through update_block_table kept them). Now every group folds them into
the row's running slot first (GDNRecoverCommitGroup.flush_deferred, same
commit kernel as the forced fold) and clears them. Unreachable on the shipped
align-mode config (a request with pending records never becomes a non-spec
row); hardening only. VLLM_GDN_RECOVER_FOLD_DEBUG=1 counts folds that found
pending records (logs every 50th call, syncs).

Tests: prefill-row case (int16/fp32 x align) + negative control (drop must
fail).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 tests/kernels/mamba/test_gdn_recover_fold.py  |  50 ++++++++-
 .../layers/mamba/ops/gdn_recover_spec.py      |  65 +++++++++++
 vllm/v1/attention/backends/gdn_attn.py        | 106 +++++++++++++++---
 3 files changed, 206 insertions(+), 15 deletions(-)

